    {
      "id": "tx-dui-second-offense",
      "name": "Driving While Intoxicated (one qualifying prior)",
      "code": "49.09(a)",
      "dpsCode": "54040010",
      "summary": "With one qualifying intoxication-offense conviction shown at trial, §49.09(a) ordinarily makes DWI Class A with a minimum confinement term of 30 days. Section 12.21 allows up to one year and a $4,000 fine. One qualifying intoxication-manslaughter prior or two qualifying other priors can instead trigger §49.09(b), a third-degree felony. Check the prior offense and its statutory qualifications.",
