  "qualifications": [
    "For qualifying final convictions Transportation Code §709.001 adds a traffic fine of $3,000 for a first conviction within 36 months, $4,500 for a second or subsequent conviction within that period, or $6,000 on the specified 0.15-or-higher trial showing. A judicial indigency finding requires waiver of all fines and costs imposed under §709.001.",
    "Effective September 1, 2025, §49.04(e) provides a state jail felony if the operator was in a school crossing zone at the time the reduced speed limit applied. Compare offense date, zone and time; the annual arrest count spans dates before and after this amendment."
  ],
